krdpserver gets an EmbedCursor option (Bool, [General] of krdpserverrc, default false).
On, the compositor paints the host's own pointer into the frames (KWin's screencast in
its Embedded cursor mode, 2 for the portal) and, once the client is streaming, the
server sends it the null system pointer so it draws none of its own; a viewer then sees
where the host's mouse is, as someone at the host's monitor does. Off, nothing changes:
krdp captures with the cursor as metadata and sends the client the pointer's shape to
draw at the client's own pointer, as before. KWin attaches no cursor metadata in
Embedded mode, so the null pointer has to be sent explicitly; Streaming is set on the
connection's own thread and may have passed before the wrapper exists, so the wrapper
both connects to stateChanged and checks the state at once. The off path is upstream's
exactly: a false argument, two if (false) tests, and the unchanged mode values.
Made against krdp 6.8.1. server/krdpserversettings.kcfg is a symlink to the kcm's.

